* Added support for adding both the x64 and ARM64 builds of a Windows Fleet-maintained app (for example, Google Chrome and Google Chrome (ARM64)) to the same fleet. Each host gets the build for its CPU, labels still apply to each build, each build keeps its own version pin, and one patch policy covers both builds. An ARM64 build is never offered to, or installed on, hosts that aren't ARM, including when it's on a software title of its own (for example, Mozilla Firefox (ARM64)). When a fleet has both builds of such an app, self-service on an ARM host lists one: the build that's installed, or the ARM64 build if neither is.
